    "open_questions": [
      "Read the figures of Conran's and Burns's theses: Picture 3's three-beat phrases, Nardis's quarter-note triplets and Jacknife's B section would give the devices their own songs, once tempos are taken from the records.",
      "Directions and Polar AC are left out of the style: their linear snare and bass drum fill every step, and the critic asks a quarter of each bar for air. Directions carries the 5:4, so no song plays it yet; Bishop's 121 under cut time is the quarter or the half note, which sound the same.",
      "Jacknife's B section: dotted quarters (2:3) or a three-beat cell (polymeter)?",
      "Read Bishop's free PDFs of Climax, Mr. Clean, Boo Ann's Grand and Backwoods Song; find bars for Forest Flower, Bitches Brew, the Jarrett trio and Special Edition's Zoot Suite."
    ]
  },
