    "roles": ["band_member", "bandleader", "composer", "educator", "author"],
    "summary": "A Chicago pianist turned drummer who played with Charles Lloyd, Bill Evans, Miles Davis (1969-71), Gateway, Keith Jarrett's trio and his own Special Edition. He called it 'multi-directional music': the time spread round the kit rather than anchored on the ride, phrases of two to five beats that cross the bar line ('washing machine time'), and grooves from Elvin-like triplets to CTI straight eighths, sambas and bossas, on high-tuned Sonor drums."
  },
